# Academia — Product Rule

## North Star

Build the operational platform for a Spanish-language academy that can scale from one director/teacher into a managed network of trained teachers.

The platform is the academy. Zoom/Google Meet is the external classroom.

## Educational models

### 1:1
- One student and one teacher.
- 60 or 90 minutes.
- Any student level.

### Group
- One teacher, maximum 15 students.
- 120 minutes.
- Once per week.
- Initially focused on native speakers training to become Spanish teachers.

## Revenue split

For each student/service:
- Academy: 15%
- Assigned teacher: 85%

The MVP may record the calculation and settlement status without automatically transferring money.

## Roles

- SUPER_ADMIN: technical/Omegon control.
- DIRECTOR: academy owner/operator.
- ADMINISTRATIVE: operational staff controlled by Director permissions.
- TEACHER: assigned teaching staff.
- STUDENT: learner.

## Authorization

Authorization must be enforced in the backend, not only hidden in the UI.

Director controls Administrative permissions.

Teacher cannot assign students to themselves.

Students can only access their own private data.

## MVP boundary

Build:
- real auth;
- role-based authorization;
- Director/Admin dashboards;
- students;
- teachers;
- assignments;
- courses/groups;
- classes/calendar;
- meeting links;
- materials;
- attendance/notes;
- basic finance;
- administrative permissions.

Do not build yet:
- native video calls;
- mobile app;
- AI;
- gamification;
- marketplace;
- internal chat;
- automated teacher payouts;
- advanced CRM;
- advanced certification.

Future buttons must visibly say `Próximamente`.

## Production principle

Prefer a small real feature over a broad fake feature.
Do not mock business-critical behavior.
Do not duplicate existing infrastructure.
